# Family A19: message identifier generators (internal/id). See hack/bakeoff.sh.
PKG=./internal/id
BENCH=BenchmarkID
REF=snowflake
AUTO_KEY=id
ADR=18
TITLE="Message identifier generator (A19)"
# Sortability and collision behaviour are correctness properties, not
# measurements: TestModel/<kind>/{sortable,collisions} gate every kind before
# it is measured.

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="ns/op & sortability -> UUIDv7"
# MATRIX=default is the only grid: internal/id has no IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX
# branch and its nine rows per kind cover generation, text and parse plus the
# concurrent generation §9.1's monotonicity claim rests on.
MATRIX=default
DECIDED_AT="Next Append Parse Text P=1 P=64 clock=fake"
DECIDED_ON="ns/op allocs/op"
# Sortability is the other half of the criterion and it is a property, not a
# metric: internal/id's own monotonicity and collision tests establish it and
# the correctness gate hack/bakeoff.sh runs first is what enforces them.
